      "writtenOn": "2025-10-09T16:22:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit: Would it be massively more complicated to take the USB3 and USB4 flags as optional strings \"usb3\" and \"usb4,\" where their absence means not enabled? Or have a positional argument valued 3 or 4? That would produce more obvious command invocations than positional boolean parameters. This is dev-facing, so usability isn\u0027t the highest priority, but we may have to use this under fire someday.\n\nAlternatively, these fields in the UCSI command appear to be redundant with the USB Mode field in the EUDO, and it seems like there is a possible invalid setting of these fields (both enabled) that is not possible in the EUDO. Would it be better to remove these as parameters and derive these UCSI fields from the EUDO? Or take a single speed argument and derive the EUDO fields from that?",
      "revId": "6b6bbc9d6b2fcedd13136c038b955dc86a11a19a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b218b7e8_1996494f",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ucsi/ppm_console.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 346,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-10T18:32:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This command is meant for testing of the PDC\u0027s response to SET_USB and to prototype USB4 entry/exit sequences.  I don\u0027t know how the PDCs will respond to an inconsistency between the enable flags and the EUDO value.\n\nUltimately, we only expect the AP to initiate a SET_USB command. This command is a stopgap measure to enable early testing.",
      "parentUuid": "39f653f6_9c5e827c",
      "revId": "6b6bbc9d6b2fcedd13136c038b955dc86a11a19a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
